    "User answered: Enters side holes; notches guide it. Maker photos/technical drawing and whole provider storyboard sheets support exterior adjustment context. No concealed side-to-side connection, numeric rope dimension or universal grip-to-notch mapping is inferred; the walkthrough includes multiple variants.",
    "Intermediate32c9 actual app inspection shows three grooves on each side and wood/granite restoration, but its cord remains outside the guides. All13wholePNG/AX/binary/ownership/cleanup records remain intermediate; final seated entry, all-eight sweep and routing acceptance are pending.",
    "A native bearing-up witness and continuous route certificate support the selected display poses; they are not a certification of mechanical equilibrium, load capacity or real-use safety.",
    "Historical gray app captures have limited installed-binary provenance. All fresh final views must bind to the final native source, sidecar, descriptor, model and installed binary.",
    "Complete original maker storyboard JPG sheets and exact retrieval/source/URL records are retained; root inspected whole sheets4and5. Do not imply all sheets were visually reviewed or fabricate content from the empty automatic-caption retrieval.",
    "The rejected nearby-triangle radial-vector fit had an approximately zero discrete nodal residual but included inadmissible material-normal directions. The independent supplement and stricter actual-feature failure are historical blockers, not final support proof. Barycentric contact forces preserve resultant and first moment; they do not establish continuum cable or global board equilibrium."
